<Project>

  <!--
    AppleDouble (`._name`) sidecars must never reach the compiler.

    WHY (docs-new/new-bugs.md, Bug 119 / Bug 131 / Bug 144): `.gitignore` already
    carries the `._*` rule, but that rule protects GIT, not the BUILD. The .NET
    SDK's default `**/*.cs` / `**/*.resx` globs read the FILESYSTEM, so a repo
    sync from macOS recreates `._Foo.cs` next to every source file and the build
    dies instantly with `CSC : error CS2015: "._Foo.cs" is a binary file instead
    of a text file` (or MSB1050 when a `._*.csproj` sidecar exists). This is not
    hypothetical: it has broken this tree once (Bug 119), MiniChessCS relapsed on
    2026-10-27 with 412 regenerated sidecars (its B118), and the .NET 11
    migration tree relapsed on 2026-11-14 (Bug 144) because this file was not
    carried over.

    This is a Directory.Build.TARGETS file, not .props, on purpose: the SDK's
    default item globs are declared in Sdk.props, which is imported BEFORE
    Directory.Build.props. A `Remove` there would run before the items it is
    meant to remove exist. Targets are imported after the project body, when the
    default items are already on the lists.

    The removals are scoped to this repository (`MSBuildThisFileDirectory`) and
    only match names that begin with `._`, so they can never hide a real source
    file.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)**/._*" />
    <Content Remove="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)**/._*" />
    <EmbeddedResource Remove="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)**/._*" />
    <None Remove="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)**/._*" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
